---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Kindling Support | Travel memories, imports, and purchases" description="Help with Kindling photo imports, memory trails, maps, voice memories, sharing, notifications, and purchases.">
  <article class="support-page section-shell">
    <header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Kindling support</p><h1>Keep the memory. Lose the friction.</h1><p>Find quick answers below or email us for private help.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:hello@maskedsyntax.com">Email Kindling support</a><p class="channel-note">Contact <a href="mailto:hello@maskedsyntax.com">hello@maskedsyntax.com</a>. Do not send personal photos, recordings, precise locations, receipts, or full Apple Account details unless we explain why they are needed.</p></header>
    <section class="troubleshooting" aria-labelledby="troubleshooting-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h2 id="troubleshooting-title">Basic troubleshooting</h2></div><ol><li>Close and reopen Kindling; an unfinished import or draft should resume.</li><li>Confirm the iPhone runs iOS 17 or later and has available storage.</li><li>For iCloud-only items, connect to the internet and try the selection again.</li><li>If audio is unavailable, check Microphone access in iPhone Settings under Apps, then Kindling.</li><li>If a purchase is missing, use Restore purchases with the Apple Account that bought it.</li><li>When reporting a problem, include the app version, iOS version, device model, import size, and stage where it occurred—without attaching personal memory content.</li></ol></section>
    <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p><h2 id="faq-title">Answers for common snags</h2><div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>Does Kindling need access to my whole photo library?</summary><div><p>No. The system picker shares only the photos and videos you select. Kindling creates protected, optimized local copies so the saved Trail remains reliable and offline-friendly.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Why is a date or place missing?</summary><div><p>Some media has no embedded date or location, and some place lookups require a network. Import still works. Open the draft to correct the date, place, grouping, or title yourself.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens to my original photos?</summary><div><p>Kindling never deletes or edits Photos-library originals. Removing a moment or trail deletes only Kindling's copy and related notes, recordings, and generated cards.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What does Kindling Pro unlock?</summary><div><p>Two saved trips are free. Pro adds unlimited trails, premium postcard and map styles, branding controls, and expanded resurfacing controls. Apple shows localized prices and trial eligibility before purchase.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How do I restore or cancel a purchase?</summary><div><p>Use Restore purchases in Kindling Settings. To cancel a subscription, open iPhone Settings, tap your name, Subscriptions, then Kindling. Apple handles refunds through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" rel="external">Report a Problem</a>.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How do I export or delete my data?</summary><div><p>Settings can prepare a JSON export, clear disposable previews, remove previous-version data, or permanently delete all Kindling data. Individual Trails can be deleted from their More menu. These actions never delete Photos-library originals.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What appears in a resurfacing notification?</summary><div><p>Lock-screen text stays generic. Details appear only after you open the app. Sensitive, hidden, archived, deleted, and “Do not resurface” moments are excluded.</p></div></details>
    </div></section>
    <section class="support-bottom"><h2>Still need help?</h2><p>Email the troubleshooting details listed above. We normally need only the Kindling version, iOS version, device model, and a description of what happened.</p><a class="button button--secondary" href="mailto:hello@maskedsyntax.com">Email hello@maskedsyntax.com</a></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
